{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"reference:89180e120791d040","name":"Lethisk-Class Armed Freighter","source":{"id":"source:reference-89180e120791d040","title":"Lethisk-Class Armed Freighter","revision":19222,"timestamp":"2024-08-25T21:33:08Z","sha256":"69bc4aad8d728770e98c85285ba5a4c57a325533c06fe3b8f755fa8586c79eca","url":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?oldid=19222","history":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?title=Lethisk-Class%20Armed%20Freighter&action=history"},"article":{"sourceId":"source:reference-89180e120791d040","blocks":[{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Reference Book: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Knights of the Old Republic Campaign Guide"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Knights_of_the_Old_Republic_Campaign_Guide"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Affiliations: ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Exchange"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Exchange","referenceId":"reference:5b7f5a0f628062b7"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["The turmoil of ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Old Republic Era"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Old_Republic_Era"}," necessitates the creation of several ",{"tag":"a","children":["Starship"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Starship"}," designs that are more heavily armed than typical civilian ships. Arakyd Industries' ",{"tag":"i","children":["Lethisk"]},"-Class Armed Freighter is a large Space Transport designed to hold its own against military forces, raiders, and other hazards in the war-torn galaxy. Though ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Old Republic"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Old_Republic","referenceId":"reference:6517b7e15507b001"}," shows stern disapproval when the ship is first introduced, Arakyd Industries is able to put the Starship into mass production thanks to a Republic defense-contract clause that allows it to sell military-grade equipment in limited quantities. The 34-meter-long ",{"tag":"i","children":["Lethisk"]},"-Class Armed Freighter features superior armor and powerful ",{"tag":"a","children":["Laser Cannons"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Laser_Cannons"},", enabling the ship to travel throughout the galaxy without ",{"tag":"a","children":["Starfighter"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Starfighter"}," escorts.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Even though Arakyd produces the ship for sale to the general public, the cost of the ",{"tag":"i","children":["Lethisk"]},"-Class keeps it out of the hands of any but the richest citizens. Wealthy families (such as the Sandal family of ",{"tag":"a","children":["Dantooine"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Dantooine","referenceId":"reference:c24e970214f5ff8b"},") snatch up most of the production run of the ",{"tag":"i","children":["Lethisk"]},"-Class Armed Freighter, but many find their way into the hands of crime lords and smugglers. Shortly after the ",{"tag":"i","children":["Lethisk"]},"-Class transport is introduced to the public, a government inquiry into Arakyd Industries uncovers a small cadre of employees that arranged for several well-known criminals (including upper-tier members of ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Exchange"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Exchange","referenceId":"reference:5b7f5a0f628062b7"},") to receive a number of first-run armed freighters at a significant discount. Following a Republic inquiry, seven Arakyd employees- including the Sector Executive of the Raioballo Sector- are sent to the spice mines of ",{"tag":"a","children":["Kessel"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Kessel","referenceId":"reference:c81eccaf20934088"}," for selling more than 30 ",{"tag":"i","children":["Lethisk"]},"-Class Armed Freighters to Exchange crime bosses.\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h4","children":["Default (Skilled)"]},"\n",{"tag":"h2","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Lethisk"]},"-Class Armed Freighter Statistics (CL 10)"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["Colossal ",{"tag":"a","children":["Space Transport"],"href":"htt